   > What the heck IS an athame?  I've scoured many a dictionary looking for it,
   > but have had no luck.

	I had the same question, and more or less assumed that it was some
   sort of staff since only wizards got to have one.  (That was a bad assumption
   since NetHack clearly treats it as a bladed weapon...)  It's actually a type
   of dagger, sometimes (usually? always?) with a "wavy" blade.  3.1 will have
   an entry for it in the database used by the '/' command:

   "	The  consecrated ritual knife of  a Wiccan  initiate (one of
   "	four  basic  tools,  together  with the  wand,  chalice  and
                                                        ^^^^^^^
   "	pentacle).   Traditionally, the  athame  is  a double-edged,
   "	black-handled,  cross-hilted   dagger  of  between  six  and
   "	eighteen inches length.

Thanks, I've wondered too. Now, what is a chalice?
/Micke - not native in English and without a dictionary...
